# Fluid Typography with clamp()

## Overview
Create responsive type scales that scale smoothly between breakpoints.

## CSS Variables

```css
@theme {
  --font-size-fluid-sm: clamp(0.875rem, 0.8rem + 0.4vw, 1rem);
  --font-size-fluid-lg: clamp(1.25rem, 1rem + 1.5vw, 2rem);
  --line-height-fluid: clamp(1.5, 1.4 + 0.2vw, 1.75);
}
```

## @utility Definition

```css
@utility text-fluid {
  font-size: clamp(1rem, 0.9rem + 0.6vw, 1.25rem);
  line-height: var(--line-height-fluid);
}
```

## Component Usage

```html
<h1 class="text-fluid font-semibold tracking-tight">Responsive Heading</h1>
```

## Calculation Formula

```
clamp(min, preferred, max)
preferred = min + (max - min) * ((100vw - minViewport) / (maxViewport - minViewport))
```

Example: `clamp(1rem, 0.9rem + 0.6vw, 1.5rem)`

## Best Practices

- Set min/max to prevent extremes
- Keep line-height fluid
- Use CSS variables for consistency
- Test at 320px, 768px, 1440px
- Pair with container queries for component-level fluidity
- Avoid too many steps; 3-5 sizes suffice
